# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/

# Smoke-test scratch output (the test itself is tracked)
_smoke_results/
_smoke_out.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Intermediate cache: ~40 MB of regenerable .npy embeddings and .parquet frames.
#
# Excluded because it is derived data, not source: every file here is rebuilt
# from data/ by the pipeline. Committing it would make the repository ~15x
# larger to save a first-run cost.
#
# Consequence: a fresh clone has a cold cache, so the first run recomputes
# everything regardless of mode ("prepared" simply finds nothing to reuse and
# falls through to computing). That path is exercised by test_scratch_smoke.py.
#
# To ship the warm cache instead, delete the next line.
results/*/cache/

# Tables and figures ARE tracked — they are the artefacts a reader wants to see
# without running anything.

# Copyright-restricted corpora: folders exist for configuration, contents do not ship
data/f1_highlights/*
!data/f1_highlights/README.md
data/f1_full/*
!data/f1_full/README.md

# Test suite: development/CI only, not part of the published artefact.
tests/

# Per-rater survey exports carry the free-text label field (t2_free_label);
# the released response data is letter choices and ratings only. The
# de-identified normalised tables (survey_responses_normalized_N*.csv) ship.
results/*/tables/survey_response_R*.csv

# Authoring/organisational material: kept locally, not part of the published
# experiment. pipeline/config.py is the single source of truth for the presets
# the notebook uses; configs/ carries the frozen record of the reported run and
# IS shipped -- the README cites it and pipeline/manuscript_tables.py reads it.
build_notebook.py
CONTENTS.md

# scratch identity-check output
results/_ident/

# Derived arrays are not distributed: the Data Availability statement ships
# aggregate results, not embeddings or projections. The manifest that documents
# the frozen experiment (hashes, shapes, identifiers) is tracked; the arrays are
# reconstructed locally from the licensed corpus.
data/f1_frozen_inputs/*.npy
results/*/cache/_superseded_offby1/
